I see there's lots of possibilites in this approach. I was thinking of
something like configurable profiles that specify race, gender, role,
name and alignment, all possibly marked for randomization. The script
would, when called, offer to choose one of these profiles or one of the
savefiles tagged with my UID. That is only a very small improvement over
nethacks built-in character generation routine (the randomized name),
but it involves less typing.
I don't really want complete randomization without any user input at
runtime, because there are days when I just don't feel like playing a
ranger.
Of course, randomized names would mean *large* lists of them, so one
.nethackrc per possible character would be somewhat extensive.

